\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Relationship between the Klein-Gordon/Helmholtz wave equation, the KG~ODE reference, and the three multislice propagators compared in this work. The KG ODE solves the second-order equation directly; WPM approximates the one-way square-root operator using local refractive-index propagators; angular spectrum multislice is the homogeneous-index propagation limit; and Fresnel multislice follows from the small-angle expansion of the angular-spectrum kernel.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method_summary}{{1}{5}{Relationship between the Klein-Gordon/Helmholtz wave equation, the KG~ODE reference, and the three multislice propagators compared in this work. The KG ODE solves the second-order equation directly; WPM approximates the one-way square-root operator using local refractive-index propagators; angular spectrum multislice is the homogeneous-index propagation limit; and Fresnel multislice follows from the small-angle expansion of the angular-spectrum kernel}{figure.1}{}}
